Version 0.90.2 (2026-09-10)

* CHANGED: Multiple behind-the-scenes improvements (part 1) - may result in new bugs :-(
* CHANGED: Restore custom external browser support and log opened resources to the console
* NEW FEATURE: Add full Qt6 support (now the default for Windows CI)
* NEW FEATURE: Drop QtMultimedia dependency and switch to miniaudio

Version 0.90.1 (2026-09-08)

* Fix unwanted in-memory database saves when moving to the tray.
* Fix application menu behavior based on the news article state.
* Fix unbounded cleanup history with publication-age retention; the feeds database (feeds.db) is now properly cleaned up on exit and respects your article retention settings.

Version 0.90.0 (2026-09-06)

* Transforms into a pure Qt5 application.
* Removes browser behavior, browser tabs/navigation/preferences and ad blocking.
* Replaces `QtWebKit` with `QTextBrowser`/`QTextDocument` (articles can still be read in the app!).
* Articles display sanitized feed-provided content; web links open externally.
* Retains reader tabs, newspaper mode, search within articles, selection/copy, zoom, printing/export, and article actions.
* Implements controlled image fetching, TLS certificate verification, supported-format negotiation and optional image diagnostics.
* Requires the installed Qt5 `QtSingleApplication` instead of the bundled copy.
* Updates Linux CI to use a Fedora 44 container and packaged dependencies.
* Updates Windows CI to actually work.
* Removes the bundled `3rdparty/qtsingleapplication` directory.
* Drops the `3rdparty/sqlite` directory, without changing its build rules.
* Fixes Windows and macOS builds (now that we've dropped built-in SQLite).
* Removes FTP support and drops `3rdparty/qftp`.
* Replaces `QzRegExp` uses with `QRegularExpression`/`QRegularExpressionMatch`, and drops `3rdparty/qupzilla`.
* Applies certain functional patches made after QuiteRSS version 0.19.4.
* Sharing methods are now dynamic and moved to an INI file, `social-networks.ini`.
* Adds Link Time Optimization (LTO) by default for all targets.
* Fixes all compilation warnings.
